# Attachments

An entry with nothing attached emits nothing at all, so the sentence reads
normally either way: \citefile{Empty:2020}right up to the full stop.

An unknown key emits nothing and warns: \citefile{Nobody:1999}

Asking for an attachment the entry hasn't got emits nothing and warns —
BibDesk numbers sparsely, so `Sparse:2021`'s only attachment is `bdsk-file-3`
and is therefore `file=1`: \citefile[file=2]{Sparse:2021}

A bare number is shorthand for the same thing: \citefile[3]{Sparse:2021}
